    <p class="lede first reveal">Every platform you build on is rented. Pinterest can change its algorithm on a Tuesday. An Instagram account can vanish overnight with no explanation and no appeal. The followers you spent a year earning were never yours — you were only ever borrowing access to them, on terms someone else controls.</p>
    <p class="reveal">There is exactly one audience the algorithm can't take from you: the people who gave you their email address. That list goes where you go. It doesn't care what Pinterest does this quarter. It is, quietly, the single most valuable asset in an online business — and the one beginners put off the longest.</p>
    <p class="reveal"><strong>You do not have a traffic problem waiting to be solved before you start a list. You have a list you should have started already.</strong> Not once you have an audience. Now — while it's small, while it's quiet, while every subscriber still feels like a person instead of a number.</p>

