    <div class="chapter reveal"><span class="bignum">05</span><div class="num">Chapter Five</div><div class="orn"><span class="d"></span></div><h2 id="send">What to send when you have nothing to sell</h2></div>
    <p class="answer reveal">When you have nothing to sell yet, send emails that are genuinely useful on their own — a tip, a short story with a lesson, an honest recommendation. You're building the habit of being opened, which is the asset every future sale depends on.</p>
    <p class="reveal">The pressure beginners feel — "I have nothing to sell, so why email?" — has it backwards. The quiet period, before you're selling, is when you earn the right to sell later. <strong>Every useful email you send while asking for nothing is a deposit you'll draw on the day you finally have something to offer.</strong></p>

