      <p>one short story with a point →</p>
      <p>one question you actually want answered →</p>
      <p>and none of it has to sell a thing.</p>
      <span class="pin-note">useful now, trusted later ♡</span>
    </div>

    <div class="chapter left reveal"><span class="bignum">06</span><div class="num">Chapter Six</div><div class="orn"><span class="d"></span></div><h2 id="income">Turning a list into income without burning it out</h2></div>
    <p class="answer reveal">A list becomes income when you sell to it occasionally and honestly — offering something that genuinely helps, framed around the reader's problem, without turning every email into a pitch. Trust spends fast when every message asks for money.</p>
    <p class="reveal">The ratio matters more than the pitch. A list that hears from you usefully most of the time will happily buy when you occasionally ask. A list that only hears from you when you're selling learns to stop opening. <strong>Sell like a trusted friend recommends — rarely, specifically, and only when it's right.</strong></p>

