    <div class="chapter reveal"><span class="bignum">07</span><div class="num">Chapter Seven</div><div class="orn"><span class="d"></span></div><h2 id="rhythm">The rhythm that keeps a list warm</h2></div>
    <p class="answer reveal">A list stays warm on a consistent, sustainable rhythm — usually one genuinely useful email a week. Consistency matters more than frequency: a list that hears from you predictably stays engaged; one that hears from you in bursts forgets you between them.</p>
    <p class="reveal">You don't need daily emails or a heroic schedule. You need a cadence you can actually keep, indefinitely. <strong>The list that gets one good email every week for a year beats the one that got thirty in a burst and then silence.</strong> Pick a rhythm you can hold, and hold it.</p>

