    <div class="chapter reveal"><div class="num">Answered</div><div class="orn"><span class="d"></span></div><h2 id="faq">Frequently asked</h2></div>
    <h3 class="reveal">How do I start an email list with no subscribers?</h3>
    <p class="reveal">Choose an email platform, create one small lead magnet that solves a narrow problem, and put a signup form where people already find you — your articles and pins. Then start writing to whoever subscribes, however few. The list grows from the habit, not from waiting.</p>
    <h3 class="reveal">How often should I email my list?</h3>
    <p class="reveal">Once a week is a reliable rhythm for most beginners — frequent enough to stay familiar, sustainable enough to keep up. What matters most is consistency; pick a cadence you can hold for a year, not one you'll abandon in a month.</p>
    <h3 class="reveal">What should I send if I'm not selling anything yet?</h3>
    <p class="reveal">Send things that are useful on their own — a tip you've learned, a short story with a lesson, an honest recommendation. Being consistently worth opening while you ask for nothing is exactly what earns you the right to sell later.</p>

